<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec copper imports up 7.2 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec copper imports up 7.2 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in December rose to 28,988 tonnes, up 7.2 percent from 27,045 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Monday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Dec 96	  Nov 96	 Dec 95</p>
<p> Total	    28,988	  29,354	 27,045</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	    13,198	  12,238	 10,880</p>
<p> U.S.		3,448	   3,772	  6,087</p>
<p> Zambia	    2,686	   1,836	  2,234</p>
<p>Imports in calendar 1996 were 360,019 tonnes, down 7.6 percent from 389,760 tonnes last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
